      "body": "> now please use your human brain and summarize what your ai-pal did please. I'm not reading through that wall of ai text\r\n\r\nbasically I found this method in your code through dynamic analysis and changed it to filter out old TLS and SSL protocols because they are deprecated and may have protocol-level weaknesses. the way I did this was by keeping the generic SSLContext.getInstance(\"TLS\"), but wrapping its SSLSocketFactory with ProtocolFilteringSslSocketFactory. this wrapper intercepts every SSL socket created by the factory and checks the protocols that the platform/provider originally enabled. ",
